  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures Mountain Goats performing fourteen songs at the Court Square Theater in Harrisonburg, Virginia, on Friday, April 4, 2003 [1]. The setlist includes rare tracks such as Alpha in Tauris, which has only eleven archived performances, and Cheshire County [1]. The show features Butter Teeth, the only archived performance of that song, and Fapps Haggles with Darnielle, which is also the sole archived version [1]. Additionally, the band plays The Anglo-Saxons, a track that appeared for the first time in twenty-seven archived shows, making it a notable inclusion [1]. The recording is forty-four minutes long and has received a four-out-of-five rating from one listener [1]. A review of this specific recording notes that it sounds like Slowest Vultures, but the reviewer states they do not care about that similarity [2]. This is the forty-first show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a previous performance on February 20, 2003, at Herrgårn [3]. The set also includes songs like Tallahassee, Neon Orange Glimmer Song, and See America Right [1].",
